@@ -1184,6 +1185,36 @@ These limits are approximate, so `vmagent` can underflow or overflow them by a s
 
 See also [cardinality explorer docs](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/single-server-victoriametrics/#cardinality-explorer).
 
+## Limiting the number of scrape targets per job
+
+By default, `vmagent` doesn't limit the number of scrape targets a single job (identified by `job_name`) can have.
+This means that a misbehaving service discovery source (for example, a broken tag filter in a cloud API
+or an overly broad catalog query) can suddenly return a huge number of targets for a single job, which
+`vmagent` will then try to scrape all at once. This can spike memory and CPU usage and degrade scraping
+for every other job running on the same `vmagent` instance.
+
+The maximum number of simultaneously scraped targets per job can be limited in the following places:
+
+* Via `-promscrape.maxScrapeTargetsPerJob` command-line flag. This limit is applied individually
+  to every job defined in the file pointed to by `-promscrape.config`.
+* Via `max_scrape_targets_per_job` config option at [scrape_config](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/sd_configs/#scrape_configs) section.
+  The `max_scrape_targets_per_job` allows overriding the `-promscrape.maxScrapeTargetsPerJob` on a per-`scrape_config` basis.
+  If `max_scrape_targets_per_job` is set to `0` or to a negative value, then it isn't applied to the given `scrape_config`,
+  even if the `-promscrape.maxScrapeTargetsPerJob` command-line flag is set.
+
+The limit applies to the total number of active targets for the job regardless of which service discovery
+mechanism (or mix of mechanisms, e.g. `kubernetes_sd_configs` combined with `static_configs`) supplied them.
+When a job's discovered target count exceeds the configured limit, `vmagent` keeps scraping only up to that
+number of targets for the job, while the remaining targets are excluded and reported as dropped targets
+with the `max scrape targets per job exceeded` reason at the same places where other scrape target status
+is already reported (see [monitoring docs](#monitoring)):
+
+* `http://vmagent-host:8429/service-discovery` shows, per job, the number of active vs total discovered targets,
+  together with a `DROPPED (max scrape targets per job exceeded)` badge for every excluded target.
+* `http://vmagent-host:8429/api/v1/targets` includes the excluded targets in the `droppedTargets` list.
+
+By default there is no limit, so existing setups are unaffected.
+
 ## Monitoring
 
 `vmagent` exports various metrics in Prometheus exposition format at `http://vmagent-host:8429/metrics` page.
